Dear Andrew,

Epoch size is set with argument windowsizes. Further, you can opt to aggregate this to 1 minute epoch in the part 5 analyses
with argument part5_agg2_60seconds. Further, time spent in MVPA is reported by default with 5, 60 and 300 second epochs in part 2. See package documentation for details:
https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/GGIR/vignettes/GGIR.html
https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/GGIR/vignettes/GGIRParameters.html

If you want to run GGIR with multiple epoch lengths, e.g. to study the effect of epoch length in more detail, then you will need to process the data multiple times.

Note that we offer GGIR training courses to help new users get started:
https://www.accelting.com/ggir-training/

Thanks,

Vincent

Dr. Vincent van Hees | Independent consultant | https://accelting.com/

